  "id": "COMPOUND:378 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between digoxin and the CD276 antigen, mediated through the Mitogen-activated protein kinase 3 (MAPK3) pathway. Digoxin is known to interact with MAPK3, which in turn is targeted by (E)-N-[amino-(3-methylbut-2-enoylamino)methylidene]-5-[(1S)-2,2-dimethyl-6-methylidenecyclohexyl]-3-methylpent-2-enamide, a compound that also targets the CD276 antigen. Additionally, digoxin is linked to MAPK3, which is also a target of Cirrhopetalanthin, another compound that directly interacts with the CD276 antigen. These findings collectively indicate that digoxin may influence the CD276 antigen through the MAPK3 signaling cascade, though the exact mechanism and the role of the second compound remain unclear. The evidence is consistent with a pathway-based interaction, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of digoxin in CD276 antigen regulation.",
